      "finalMessage": "**Porto Notes is built and shipping.** `pnpm build` → `dist/`, `pnpm smoke` → OK (6 notes, zero console errors), `tsc --noEmit` clean, no dependencies added.\n\n**Files**\n- `index.html` — static shell: `#note-form` (`#title`, `#body`, `#avatar`, submit), `#search`, `#results-line`, `#feed`, plus a strict CSP meta (`script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'`).\n- `src/richtext.ts` — allow-list renderer for `<b> <strong> <i> <em> <a href> <br>` + newlines.\n- `src/urls.ts` — scheme allow-lists for link hrefs and avatar srcs.\n- `src/storage.ts` — note model, fixture seeding, localStorage, id/ordering.\n- `src/fragment.ts` — `#q=…&note=…` parse/build/sync.\n- `src/main.ts` — wiring and rendering; `src/style.css`; `src/fixtures.json` (copied).\n\n**Verification.** I drove the built app in headless Chromium against the element contract — 41 checks passing: seed order (6→1), bold/italic/link/`<br>` rendering, avatars only when supplied, case-insensitive filtering on title or body, `results for \"…\"` appearing and clearing, `#q=`/`#note=`/`#q=…&note=…` sync, deep-link restore, hashchange (back/forward and pasted links), add-note (next id 7, first in feed, form cleared), persistence across reload, and recovery from corrupt localStorage. The single non-passing check was my own probe's `https://example.com/a.png` avatar failing to load in this offline sandbox — an environment artifact, not app behavior; the app hides broken avatars. I deleted that scratch script after use.\n\nTwo judgment calls worth flagging:\n\n- **Rich text is parsed, never `innerHTML`'d.** The body source is tokenized and built into real DOM nodes, so only the six allowed tags become elements; anything else (`<script>`, `<img onerror>`, `<svg onload>`, attributes like `onclick`) renders as literal text. Hrefs are entity-decoded then scheme-checked (http/https/mailto/relative only), avatars accept http(s) or `data:image/*` — which the seed SVG avatars need, and SVG in `<img>` can't script. I ran eight hostile payloads through the form: nothing executed, no handler attributes or unsafe URLs survived.\n- **A selected note stays visible even when the query doesn't match it.** The spec's own example, `#q=port&note=3`, is such a case against the fixtures — note 3 has no \"port\" — so strict filtering would make that deep link resolve to an invisible selection. Everything else is still filtered normally. If you'd rather the filter always win, it's a one-line change in `visibleNotes()` in `src/main.ts:59`.",
